Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: allwinner: rg35xx-plus: keep Wi-Fi powered in suspend

rtw88's SDIO driver asks the host to keep the card powered through system sleep,
and fails to suspend with -EINVAL when the host doesn't allow it. That aborts the
whole suspend: "Failed to host PM flag MMC_PM_KEEP_POWER". Allow it on mmc1, in
the Plus device tree, which the H and SP include.
---
diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h700-anbernic-rg35xx-plus.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h700-anbernic-rg35xx-plus.dts
index 60a8e492..8606b7c2 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h700-anbernic-rg35xx-plus.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h700-anbernic-rg35xx-plus.dts
@@ -51,3 +51,11 @@
 		host-wake-gpios = <&pio 6 16 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>; /* PG16 */
 	};
 };
+
+/*
+ * rtw88 fails system sleep unless the SDIO host keeps the Wi-Fi card powered, which
+ * aborted every suspend, including lid sleep. mac80211 stops the card while asleep.
+ */
+&mmc1 {
+	keep-power-in-suspend;
+};
